    "md5": "4ff0030b4925391e5ab924f1b8d1128d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1949,
    "chunk_text": "As from 01.01.2018 each employee covered and boundby this Agreement shall be paid upon and subject to theother terms and conditions herein contained a monthlysalary which comprises the following components:\n\n5.1 Fixed Component\n\n(i) Revised basic salary as set out in the\u201cAnnexure 1\u201d hereto. (Increments will begranted continuously notwithstanding themaximum point given in the salary scales).\n\n(ii) The revised basic salary in \u201cAnnexure 1\u201dhereto will be paid in the years 2018, 2019and 2020 on compounding basis, in thefollowing manner:\n\na. 70% with effect from 01st January2018\n\nb. 15% out of the gross salary as at 31-12-2018, with effect from 01st\n\nJanuary 2019\n\nc. balance amount to match the industrylevel, with effect from 01st January2020\n\n(iii) In the event, the Bank achieves theminimum capital requirement of Rs. five(05) Billion on or before 31sl December2018, the Bank shall pay the revised salaryin Annexure 1 hereto, as follows:\n\na. 70% with effect from 01st January2018\n\nb. balance 30% with effect from 01st\n\nJanuary 2019\n\n5.2 Allowances\n\n(a) In addition to the basic salary, the followingallowances will be paid, effective from01.01.2018:\n\n(i) Cost of Living Allowance based onthe CCPI varying in the particularmonth.\n\n(ii) Rent Allowance as per item (b) below\n\n(iii) 10% on the aggregate of the Basicsalary + Rent Allowance + Cost ofLiving Allowance.\n\n(b) The rent allowance will be 20% of the BasicSalary.\n\n5.3 Variable Component\n\nBasis of determination of variable componentwhich consist of cost of living allowance shall bedetermined in the course of time.\n\n6. ANNUAL INCREMENT\n\nThe annual increment payable to the employees for theperiod 2018 to 2020 shall be on the basis specified inthe revised salary scale in \u201cAnnexure 1\u201d hereto.\n\n7. CONVERSION OF THE BASIC SALARY\n\n(a) The Basic Salaries of all employees will beconverted to the revised scale by applying the stepfor step (point by point) method of conversion."
