    "chunk_text": "The Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n\u0dc1\u0dd3 \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u0db4\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dd3 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0dca \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0da7\u0dca \u0db4\u0dad\u0dba\n\n\u0d85\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2\n\n\u0d85\u0d82\u0d9a 2126/5 - 2019 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dc3 03 \u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0db3\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dcf - 2019.06.03 No. 2126/5 \u2013 MONDAY, JUNE 03, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460) Notice under Section 7 My Ref No.: BD/HP/LND4/LAQ/78 Ministry of Land Reference.: 4-38/2016/PC/365 I, hereby give notice under Sub-Section (1) of Section 07, of the Land Acquisition Act, as amended by the land Acquisition (Amendment) Act, No. 28 of 1964 that the Government intends to acquire the following land /servitude* which is required for a public purpose. Description of the land or Servitude to be acquired:- Allotments below name land in total extent of about 1.2091 Hectares shown in Town Survey Preliminary Plan No. 28, Supplement No. 69, Sheet No. 74 and dated 2019.02.18, prepared by the Senior Superintendent of Surveys, Badulla District on behalf of the Surveyor General, situated in town of Diyathalawa in the Grama Niladhari Division of No. (63B) Diyathalawa and Minor Division of Mahapalatha Korale in the Division of Haputhale, in the District of Badulla in Uva Province 1. Lot No. 1415 Name of the land: Poliskanda Pathana, Dodamwaththa Pathana; Land use: Estate, 50-60 years old tea and mixed farming; Claimant: State; Extent: 0.0049 Hectare.\n\nBoundaries : North: Lot No. 1420, 1418 and 1417; East: Lot No. 1417; South: Lot Nos. 1417 and 1420; West: Lot No. 1420.\n\n2. Lot No. 1416 Name of the land: Poliskanda Pathana, Dodamwaththa Pathana; Land use: Estate, 50-60 years old tea and mixed farming; Claimant: State; Extent: 0.0230 Hectare.\n\nBoundaries : North and East: Lot No. 1417; South: Lot Nos. 1417, 1418 and 1420; West: Lot No. 1420.\n\n3. Lot No. 1420 Name of the land: Akadiya waththa or Dabagoda waththa; Land use: Estate, 60-70 years old tea and mixed farming; Claimant: Land Reform Commision; Extent: 1.1548 Hectares."
