    "chunk_text": "3. No person shall serve as a skipper in a multiday local fishing boat having aforementioned specificationswithout obtaining a Certificate of Competence issued by the Director-General of the Department of Fisheries and AquaticResources (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cDirector-General\u201d) or a coxswain license issued by a recognized maritimetraining institute for the purpose.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'06'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 03.06.20192A\n\n(a) not be less than eighteen (18) years of age as at the date on which the relevant written or oral test as thecase may be, is to be held ;\n\n(b) have, not less than two (2) years experience on a multiday local fishing boat referred to above, at the sea,either as a skipper or as a crew member ; and\n\n(c) have completed a fishing vessel skipper training programme of not less than one (1) week duration, in anyrecognized institute approved by the Director - General.\n\n5. The application for a Certificate of Competence shall be accompanied by the following documents :-\n\n(a) a fitness certificate issued by a recognized medical practioner or a recognized medical institute includingthe hearing and visual state of the applicant ;\n\n(b) a certificate of competence issued by any one of the following institutions, namely -\n\n(i) Ocean University of Sri Lanka, established under the Ocean University of Sri Lanka Act, No. 31 of2014 ;\n\n(ii) Colombo International Nautical and Engineering College recognized as a degree awarding instituteunder the Universities Act, No. 16 of 1978 ;\n\n(iii) Mahapola Academy established under the Sri Lanka Ports Authority Act, No. 51 of 1979 ; or\n\n(iv) any other institute recognized for the purpose by the Director-General.\n\ncertifying that the applicant has undergone training successfully as a skipper in a fishing vessel for aperiod of not less than one (1) week ; and"
