    "chunk_text": "(iv) any other institute recognized for the purpose by the Director-General.\n\ncertifying that the applicant has undergone training successfully as a skipper in a fishing vessel for aperiod of not less than one (1) week ; and\n\n6. Every application for a Certificate of Competence under these regulations shall be sent, addressed to theDirector-General, and shall be in the form specifed in Schedule I hereto.\n\n7. Every eligible applicant shall be informed of the venue and the date of the oral or written test as the case maybe, in writing by the Director-General at least one week before such date.\n\n8. The Director-General may, from time to time made amendments to the syllabus applicable to the oral orwritten test as the case may be, to be conducted under these regulations in order to maintain high standards of such test.\n\n9. The Director-General shall, upon being satisfied that the candidate has achieved the required standards at theoral or written test as the case may be, issue a certificate of competence to the successful candidate within a period of twoweeks from such test.\n\n10. The Director-General shall issue a skipper license in the form specified in Schedule II hereto, to any applicantwho obtained the certificate of competence referred to in regulation 9 upon payment of the license fee referred to inSchedule III hereto.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'06'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 03.06.20193A\n\n11. Any candidate who is unable to achieve the required standards at the oral or written test may be granted afurther period of time by the Director-General to undergo training at any of the institutions referred to in regulation 5(b)and such candidate shall be given only two opportunities to sit for such oral or written test.\n\n12. In these regulations -"
