    "chunk_text": "THE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON\n\n1956 REVISED EDITION\n\nof the one part\n\nMr. P. D. P. Sisila Kumara, No. B-12, 500 Houses - Scheme, Kiriwandala, Puwakpitiya, Avissawella.\n\nandof the other part\n\nSTATEMENT OF MATTER IN DISPUTE\n\nThe matter in dispute between the aforesaid parties is \u2013\n\nWhether Mr. P. D. P. Sisila Kumara had been caused injustice by being the only person not to be given relief from his punishments, when6 out of the 7 persons who worked in the Ceylon Electricity Board against whom a disciplinary inquiry was conducted with regard to thedeath of employee S. V. S. Rathnasiri and accident of employee Hemal Jagath Kumara that had occurred while being engaged in a 33,000 highvoltage maintenance duty in the Customer Service Centre area of Ingiriya on 31.01.2013 had been given relief following their appeal againstthe punishments given and if such injustice had been caused, to what relief he is entitled.\n\nA. WIMALAWEERA,Commissioner General of Labour.\n\nDated at the Office of the Commissioner General of Labour,Colombo,This 21st day of May, 2019.\n\n06 - 514\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
