    "chunk_text": "Ministry of Internal & Home Affairs andProvincial Councils & Local Government,\u201cSuhurupaya\u201d,Sri Subhuthipura Road,Battaramulla.20th May, 2019.\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A - PG 4543\u2014 517 (06/2019)\n\nL.D.B. 10/2015\n\nIMMIGRANTS AND EMIGRANTS ACT (Chapter 351)\n\nREGULATIONS made by the Minister of Internal and Home Affairs and Provincial Councils and Local Government underSection 52, read with Section 23 of the Immigrants and Emigrants Act, (Chapter 351) and approved by Parliament.\n\nWAJIRA ABEYWARDANA,Minister of Internal & Home Affairs and ProvincialCouncils and Local Government.\n\nColombo,20th May, 2019.\n\nRegulations\n\nThe Immigrants and Emigrants Regulations 1956, published in the Supplement to the Ceylon Government GazetteNo. 10,896 of February 24, 1956 are hereby amended as follows :-\n\n1. in regulation 8 -\n\n(1)in paragraph (1) by the substitution for the words \u2018\u2018 furnish such Number of copies of the photograph orof the finger- prints or of both,\u201d of the words \u2018\u2018 furnish such Number of copies of the photograph or ofthe bio metrics or of both,\u2019\u2019;\n\n(2)in paragraph (2), by the substitution for the words, \u201cor of the finger-prints furnished\u201d of the words, \u201c orof the bio metrics furnished\u201d.\n\n2. by the insertion immediately after regulation 10, of the following new regulation :-\n\n\u201c10A. (1) Any person who contravenes the condition which specifies the period of stay in any visagranted or issued to that person, by overstaying in Sri Lanka, shall be required to pay a penelty of UnitedStates Dollars 500, in addition to the applicable visa fee for the perdiod of over stay.\n\n(2)Notwithstanding the provisions of paragraph (1), the prescribed Authority may grant a grace period -\n\n(a)of two days at the port of depature to a person referred to in paragraph (1) ; or\n\n(b)seven days when applying for an extension of the period of stay specifed in the visa from theDepartment of Immigration and Emigration."
