    "chunk_text": "IV ^wd& jeks fldgi \u2013 YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2018'04'09Part IV (B) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 09.04.20181A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2127$10 - 2019 cqks ui 11 jeks w\u00d5yrejdod - 2019'06'11No. 2127/10 - TUESDAY JUNE 11, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nFILLING OF A VACANCY IN THE OFFICE OF MEMBER OF THE MAHIYANGANAPRADESHIYA SABHA UNDER SECTION 66A(1)(a) OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES ELECTIONSORDINANCE (CHAPTER 262)\n\nWHEREAS the office of member of Mahiyangana pradeshiya Sabha has fallen vacant by reason of Resignation ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Leader of the Independent Group to which Wanninayaka Mudiyanselage SamanPushpakumara Wanninayaka the member belonged, was required by me under Section 66 A (1)(a) of the aforesaid ordinance,to decide upon the member of that Ward No. 12, Dambarawa of Mahiyangana Pradeshiya Sabha who belongs to suchIndependent Group and is not disqualified under Section 9 of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262)and who shall be declared elected as a member within a period of thirty (30) days ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Leader of the aforesaid Independent Group has communicated his decision to nominateAththanayaka Mudiyanselage Sumanarathna to fill such vacancy ;\n\nNOW THEREFORE, I, H. I. R. Hathurusinghe, Returning Officer of the Mahiyangana Pradeshiya Sabha, acting interms of Section 66A(1)(a) of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262) do hereby declare that AththanayakaMudiyanselage Sumanarathna was elected as the member of the Ward No. 12 Dambarawa of Mahiyangana PradeshiyaSabha.\n\nH. I. R. HATHURUSINGHA,Returning Officer,Mahiyangana pradeshiya Sabha.District Election Office,Badulla,10th June, 2019.\n\n06 - 745\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART IV (B) \u2014 LOCAL GOVERNMENT\n\nNotices under the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance"
