    "chunk_text": "1AIII fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'05'27PART III \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 27.05.2019\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nREVOCATION ORDER UNDER SECTION 39 (1)\n\nThe servitude of the allotment of land described in detail in the OrderNo. 145 of 2014 dated 23.06.2014 made under the Proviso (a) toSection 38 of the Land Acquisition Act (Chapter 460) and publishedin the Gazette Extra Ordinary No. 1868/51 dated 25.06.2014 isvested in the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka. Therefore,I Gayantha Karunatilleke, Minister of Lands and ParliamentaryReforms, by virtue of powers vested in me under Section 39(1) ofthe Land Acquisition Act, do hereby revoke the aforesaid Order 145of 2014 dated 23.06.2014 published in the Gazette Extra OrdinaryNo. 1868/51 dated 25.06.2014.\n\nGayantha Karunatilleke,Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms.\n\nMy Ref. No.: 4-3/9/2011/WS/328.Divisional Secretary\u2019s No.: fod$b$1$w;a$104'Ministry of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms,\u201cMihikatha Medura\u201d,Rajamalwatta Road,Battaramulla.29th May, 2019.\n\nSchedule\n\n1. Description of the Land.\u2013 Allotment of land called\n\nVoganwaththa - Deegalla Division in total extent of about 0.3224\n\nHectare depicted in the Advanced Tracing No. Ka/DDN/12/55 dated\n\n26.09.2012 prepared by the Surveyor General, situated in the Village\n\ncalled Nebada in the Divisional Secretary\u2019s Division of Dodangoda\n\nin Kalutara District of Western province and bounded as follows:\n\n2. Description of the Servitude.\u2013 Acquisition of servitude for\n\nthe construction of the Access road to the Nebada Water Tower of\n\n600 cubic meters and the office of the Officer in charge, under the\n\nIntegrated Water Supply Scheme, Aluthgama, Mathugama,\n\nAgalawaththa.:\n\n01. Lot \u2018A\u2019 \u2013 Voganwaththa, Deegalla Division \u2013 Extent:\n\nAbout 0.3224 Hectare\n\nNorth, East and South: Voganwaththa-Deegalla Division claimed\n\nby Kotagala Plantation Company Ltd; West: Road and Voganwaththa-"
