    "chunk_text": "Mr. Obadage Lelarathne No. 242, Sri Sobitha Mawatha, Nagoda, Kalutara to be the arbitrator and refer the aforesaid dispute to him for\n\nsettlement by arbitration.\n\nRAVINDRA SAMARAWEERA,\n\nMinister of Labour and Trade Union Relations.\n\nColombo,\n\n06th June, 2019.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON\n\n1956 REVISED EDITION\n\nof the one part\n\nMr. S. A. Daya Keerthi Bandara, No. 250, Koswatta, Halmillawewa.\n\nandof the other part\n\nMerchant Bank of Sri Lanka and Finance PLC, 17th Floor, Bank of Ceylon Building, No. 28, St. Michael\u2019s Road, Colombo - 03.\n\nSTATEMENT OF MATTER IN DISPUTE\n\nThe matter in dispute between the aforesaid parties is \u2013\n\nWhether Mr. S. A. Daya Keerthi Bandara who had worked in the Merchant Bank of Sri Lanka and Finance PLC had been caused injustice\n\nby non-acceptance of his resignation letter and conducting a disciplinary inquiry and considering him as a resigned employee without giving\n\nthe decision of the disciplinary inquiry and if so, to what relief he is entitled.\n\nA. WIMALAWEERA,\n\nCommissioner General of Labour.\n\nDated at the Office of the Commissioner General of Labour,\n\nColombo,\n\nThis 31st day of May, 2019.\n\n06 - 834\n\nI fldgi: (I) fPoh \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'06'13PART I: SEC. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 13.06.20193A\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/04/2019/139.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON( 1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nOrder under Section 4(1)\n\nWHEREAS an industrial dispute in respect of the matter specified in the statement of the Commissioner of Labour which accompanies thisorder exists between,\n\nof the one part\n\nLanka Estate and Industrial Workers\u2019s Union, No. 457, Dr. Colvin R. De Silva Mawatha, Colombo 02\n\nandof the other part\n\n01. Dole Lanka (Private) Limited, 12th Floor, Parkland Building, No. 33, Park Street, Colombo 02."
